# NON-REGRESSION PIN — ⚠ GREEN BEFORE AND AFTER THE ALIAS-RESOLUTION FIX.
# This fixture is NOT red-verifiable against the pre-fix compiler, and it is
# labelled as such deliberately. What it pins is stated below; do not read it
# as coverage for the alias-spelling defect (the four
# `cow_alias_spelled_*` fixtures carry that).
#
# CELL: TEMPORAL ORDER — the alias is bound BEFORE the root is reassigned,
# and the view is taken AFTER.
#
#     Vector[String] alias = v      # alias aliases v's storage
#     v = []                        # reassign: severs, alias takes its own copy
#     String s = alias.get(0).unwrap()   # view taken AFTER the sever
#     ... grow the NEW v ...
#     print(s)                      # must still be the OLD element
#
# WHAT IT PINS, AND WHAT IT CANNOT: the END-TO-END temporal behaviour only.
# The sever gives `alias` its own copy of the pre-reassignment value, the
# view taken afterwards reads that copy, and the new `v` goes its own way.
# That is worth pinning, and it is all this program pins.
#
# ⚠ NO BREAK-THE-MECHANISM RED WAS FOUND FOR IT, and the reason is a property
# of the program rather than a gap in the search. After the sever, `s`
# borrows into the buffer `alias` now owns outright, and NOTHING MUTATES
# `alias` for the rest of the program -- only `v` grows. A borrow whose
# buffer is never touched cannot dangle, so no provenance decision is
# load-bearing here and no amount of breaking the provenance machinery can
# change this program's output.
#
# Measured, so the next reader does not repeat it -- three separate breaks,
# each rebuilt and run, all three leaving this fixture rc 0 `hello|1|65`:
#   1. deleting `unset_ownership(builder, alias)` before the materialize in
#      `cow_sever_all_aliases_from`;
#   2. suppressing the `register_local` name rebind onto the fresh owned
#      local in `cow_materialize_alias`;
#   3. both at once.
# An earlier version of this header asserted (1) as the mechanism AND as the
# procedure for seeing this go red. Both were false. That is worse than
# saying nothing: it hands the next engineer a command that silently does
# nothing, which reads as confirmation.
#
# ⊕ For the temporal cell WITH a live mechanism and a fire count, see
# `cow_alias_severed_then_alias_grows.gg` -- same shape, but the alias's own
# buffer reallocs after the view is taken, so the rescue must fire and the
# emitted GIR is asserted to contain it.
#
# The two lengths are printed as well as the string: they pin that the sever
# gave `alias` its own 1-element copy while `v` went on to 65, i.e. that CoW
# value semantics held across the reassignment.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(mk("hel", "lo"))
    Vector[String] alias = v
    v = []
    v.push(mk("new", "one"))
    String s = alias.get(0).unwrap()
    int i = 0
    while i < 64:
        v.push(mk("fill", "er"))
        i = i + 1
    print(s)
    print(alias.len())
    print(v.len())
